900 GOSUB 6100:BM$="Helped by Lands, Susanna brought David back to her room. They laid him on\the bed, and he immediately fell asleep.":GOSUB 5100
1000 BM$="David was sleeping like a corpse.":GOSUB 5100
1005 BM$="Mr. and Mrs. Lands went home to prepare for their guard duty.":GOSUB 5100
1006 BM$="Susanna also left the room. She was gathering the tools she needed to\cast a spell that would protect David from the King of the North.":GOSUB 5100
1010 BM$="After a while, David came to his senses. He was alone in the room.":GOSUB 5100
1020 BM$="He looked around. The room was illuminated by candles.":GOSUB 5100
1030 BM$="David: ...This is Susanna's room... So I was sleeping... But what about those\corpses...? Was it another nightmare...?":GOSUB 5100
1040 BM$="David: ...Susanna's a dark sorceress... She killed them to revive the blood of\the Devil King in my veins...":GOSUB 5100
1045 BM$="David: ...Those two detectives and their clients are northern tribesmen...\Nightmare or not, something's about to happen...":GOSUB 5100
1050 BM$="David: ...I must talk to Susanna... If she really is a dark sorceress, then...":GOSUB 5100
1060 BM$="David felt uneasy about seeing Susanna. The nightmare caused him to feel\different about her.":GOSUB 5100
1070 COMMON FO:GOSUB 6110:BM$="He lit a lamp and walked out of the room.":GOSUB 5100
1075 GOSUB 9000:GOSUB 6120:BM$="He had not learned the layout of the castle yet. He went downstairs,\entering the dining room.":GOSUB 5100:'
1080 GOSUB 6130:BM$="The candles in the dining room were lit, but Susanna was not there.":GOSUB 5100
1085 GOSUB 6140:BM$="He returned to the corridor. For some reason, he recalled his nightmare.":GOSUB 5100
1090 BM$="David: ...In my dream, at the end of the corridor there was another path to\the right...":GOSUB 5100
1100 BM$="As if to confirm whether it was merely a dream, David walked down the\corridor. Then, he saw a light coming from his right.":GOSUB 5100
1120 GOSUB 6150:BM$="The moment he turned right, he felt as if he was back in his nightmare.":GOSUB 5100
1130 BM$="Candles were lit along the walls. At the end of the corridor was a door... the\same door he saw in his nightmare.":GOSUB 5100
1140 BM$="David: In my nightmare, beyond that door there were stairs that led to the\basement... Am I still dreaming...?":GOSUB 5100
1150 GOSUB 6160:BM$="David ran down the corridor and stopped in front of the door.":GOSUB 5100
1155 GOSUB 6170:BM$="Then, he opened it.":GOSUB 5100
1160 BM$="As he feared, there were stairs that led to a basement, lit by candles.":GOSUB 5100
1170 GOSUB 6180:BM$="David walked down the stairs.":GOSUB 5100
1175 GOSUB 6190:BM$="When he reached a door, he stopped to think.":GOSUB 5100
1180 BM$="David: ...If this is like my nightmare, beyond this door would be... two men,\lying in a pool of blood... Susanna and the sorcerers...":GOSUB 5100
1190 BM$="David was afraid to open the door. He would rather go back, but something\compelled him to see the truth with his own eyes...":GOSUB 5100
1200 CM=2:CM$(1)="He decided to open the door.":CM$(2)="He decided to return to the room and wait for Susanna."
